WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:02.760
- Do you see the beauty of it?

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:06.270
My swift and terrible sword,
and the Earth will crack

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.870
with the weight of your failure.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:11.160
When the dust settles,
the only thing living

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.990
in this world, will be metal.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.930
In 2015, the world
reeled from attacks from

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.160
enhanced individuals.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.280
It was not prepared for
the tragedy in Sokovia,

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.230
under the leadership of Ultron,

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.220
a robot army descended
on the peaceful town

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.700
of Novigrad, Sokovia, a province known

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.373
for its wheat production
and fine woolen goods.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.470
In a battle that pitted
sibling against sibling,

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:43.824
the otherwise sleepy town
of Novigrad was levitated

00:00:43.824 --> 00:00:45.560
in to the sky.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.740
Hundreds of thousands
of Sokovians perished,

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.800
and the world was forever changed.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.660
But in the wake of the tragedy,

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:58.430
countries around the world
rallied around a common cause,

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.610
in response to the Sokovian tragedy

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:04.750
and the supervillian Ultron,
the world knew what it needed,

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.853
to regulate enhanced individuals.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:12.720
That is legally problematic.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.837
(guitar playing)

00:01:15.837 --> 00:01:19.070
Hey LegalEagles, it's time
to think like a lawyer.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:20.850
Welcome back to Laws
Broken, where an attorney

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.590
destroys your favorite childhood movies,

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:25.080
by showing you how illegal everything is,

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.530
because everything is illegal.

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:29.770
Today we're talking
about the Sokovia Accords

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:31.300
from "Captain America's Civil War"

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.400
and the rest of the "Avengers" movies.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.570
We're going to pretend
that it is an actual

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:38.580
binding, legal document and analyze it

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.370
in far, far, too much detail.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:43.380
For better or worse, in the
wake of the Ultron disaster,

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.600
countries worldwide,
through the United Nations,

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.260
signed the Sokovia Accords.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.780
The Sokovia Accords are
a phone book sized set

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:53.210
of regulations aimed squarely
at the Avengers personally,

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.390
and the organization S.H.E.I.L.D.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:58.890
It seeks to limit the
so-called enhanced individuals,

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:00.500
including registration components,

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:03.900
monitoring components, and
imprisonment components.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.920
I'm using the version
of the Sokovia Accords

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.430
found at the Marvel Cinematic
Universe Fandom Wiki,

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:11.100
which you can find at the link below.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.740
Importantly, some of the
provisions only apply

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.900
to signatories of the Sokovia Accords,

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.100
while other provisions apply
to all enhanced individuals,

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.570
whether they sign or not.

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:23.540
This is quite the constitutional problem.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:26.150
So because this is
obviously the most important

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:29.220
legal analysis that I could
possibly be doing right now,

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.040
I put together 10 reasons
why the Sokovia Accords

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.020
raise constitutional questions.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.920
But first, I want to talk
about the legal landscape

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.880
in general, specifically
whether the Sokovia Accords

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.420
would even be U.S. law and number two,

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.890
what would the legal
framework be for dealing

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:45.890
with enhanced individuals in the absence

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.510
of the Sokovia Accords?

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:50.230
So first, let's talk about
the Accords in general.

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.900
An accord is not a U.S. law,

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.030
I assume what the Marvel
writers meant here is that

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:57.310
the Sokovia Accords are
an international treaty

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.020
that the U.S. has signed.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:02.890
But just because 177
countries signed an agreement,

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:05.830
doesn't actually make it
law in the United States.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.100
In the case of a treaty,
the Senate has to approve

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.760
the treaty by a 2/3 vote
under Article II, Section 2

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:12.880
of the Constitution.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.090
And there are tons of examples of treaties

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:17.990
that the U.S. has signed
but not actually ratified,

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.600
that includes the International
Criminal Court Treaty,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.550
the Comprehensive Nuclear Test Ban Treaty,

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:25.640
the Kyoto Protocol, and
the Treaty of Versailles,

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.600
basically the U.S. is
still in World War I.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.020
But for the sake of
argument, let's assume that

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:33.490
the U.S. Senate has, in fact,
ratified the Sokovia Accords,

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:35.300
it's more fun that way, in any event,

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.560
even when treaties are ratified,

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.980
they cannot violate the U.S. Constitution,

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.780
and, in fact, this was
an issue when the U.S.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.840
adopted NATO, because it was thought

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.810
that the Mutual Defense
Treaty would violate

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:48.000
Congress' right to declare war.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.570
But before we get to analyzing
the actual Sokovia Accords

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:53.730
themselves, we have to
examine the status quo ex ante

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.040
of U.S. criminal law and tort law.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.020
Captain America chafes at the restrictions

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.975
of the Sokovia Accords, but
it's not like in the absence

00:03:59.975 --> 00:04:03.380
of the Accords, he'd be
allowed to operate domestically

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:04.600
in the United States.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:08.860
Vigilantes are illegal, as
we discussed in the video

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:11.710
on the "Dark Knight" and all
the laws that Batman broke.

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:14.060
You can't just go around
getting in to fights,

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.480
even for a good cause.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.160
The justification of
self-defense generally doesn't

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.340
apply when you intentionally
put yourself in harm's way.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:23.700
And all of these enhanced
individuals are using

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.780
deadly force, which almost
always carries with it

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:29.840
a duty to retreat if
you are able to do so.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:31.740
Of course, U.S. law
doesn't necessarily apply

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.500
to the Avenger's actions in Sokovia

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.100
and other foreign countries.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:37.370
But the fact of the matter
is, they are often operating

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:39.810
domestically where U.S. law does apply.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:42.130
Don't even get me started
about issues of federalism

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:45.330
because even if enhanced
individuals were allowed,

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:47.540
under the Sokovia Accords
on the federal level,

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:49.190
there's still all the state laws

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:50.770
that prohibit their actions.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:53.120
And there's no way
federal law would preempt

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:55.750
garden variety state laws
about criminal conduct.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:56.807
Now you might argue that
it seems like the Avengers

00:04:56.807 --> 00:05:00.230
in S.H.E.I.L.D. are operating
as an arm of the government,

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:03.210
essentially like mercenaries,
which might have given them

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.530
legal cover under the battle of New York,

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.600
but if that's so, that
they're operating as an arm

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.710
of the U.S. government, that
carries with it all kinds

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:11.970
of constitutional protections
and that doesn't get them

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:12.803
out of trouble.

00:05:12.803 --> 00:05:15.310
By the way, Tony Stark created Ultron,

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:18.040
and effectively Ultron is
his product entered in to

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.880
the stream of commerce,
so Tony Stark is probably

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.920
personally liable on a product's liability

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.700
or negligence theory for all
the damage that Ultron did.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.550
And since this is a Marvel movie,

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:30.520
I put an after-credits
bonus scene about that topic

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:32.070
at the end of this video.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:33.910
But the fact that the
writers even considered

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.710
any of these legal issues is why

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.920
the adoption of Sokovia Accords

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.360
is the best scene in the MCU.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.380
- Actually the best scene in
the MCU is the after party

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.800
from "Age of Ultron"
because of how effectively

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:48.340
it uses a light, fun
moment between the Avengers

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:50.810
to reveal important
information about the main

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:53.300
characters while still
being a funny scene.

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.330
- Actually the best scene in the MCU

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:58.140
is the I'm Always Angry" scene
from the first "Avengers"

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:00.050
because it's just so iconic.

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:02.850
- Well actually, I'd say that
the best scene in the MCU

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:06.057
is the military propaganda
montage in the original

00:06:06.057 --> 00:06:09.480
"Captain America" movie
because no other scene is so

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:13.413
subversive, over-the-top,
and hilarious all ...

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:17.460
- Yeah, this is my court,
objections overruled.

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:20.640
But let's ignore those
issues and let's talk about

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:23.620
the 10 biggest problems
with the U.S. version

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:25.540
of the Sokovia Accords.

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:28.950
So in order of ascending
constitutional infirmity,

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.670
let's start with the
compelled speech portion

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:32.960
of the Sokovia Accords.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:35.177
The Sokovia Accords state, and I quote,

00:06:35.177 --> 00:06:37.540
"Any enhanced individual who agree to sign

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:39.410
must register with the
United Nations and provide

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:42.077
biometric data such as
fingerprints and DNA samples..."

00:06:42.077 --> 00:06:44.720
"Those with secret
identities must reveal their

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:48.470
legal names and true identities
to the United Nations..."

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:51.960
This is a classic provision
of compelled speech,

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:53.590
some of which applies to signatories

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:56.100
and some of which does
not apply to signatories.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.260
But forcing individuals to give up their

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:01.420
secret identities is the
government compelling you

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:04.610
to make a certain kind of speech.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:05.533
- I am Iron Man.

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:09.030
- And if the first amendment has a problem

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.350
with the government
restricting certain speech,

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:13.910
you can imagine that it
is doubly problematic

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.900
if it forces individuals to
make a certain kind of speech.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:19.100
For example, in the Supreme Court case

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:22.040
of West Virginia School
Board vs. Barnette,

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.990
the Supreme Court said that
a school could not force

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:27.810
students to stand and salute the flag.

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:29.380
That was compelled speech.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:31.590
And in the same way that
you can't force individuals

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:33.889
to stand up and salute the flag,

00:07:33.889 --> 00:07:37.030
you can't force people to give
up their secret identities

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:39.460
and provide biometric
data and fingerprints

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:40.500
to the U.S. government.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.960
Number two, forced registration sounds

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.770
a lot like internment.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:47.590
The Sokovia Accords requires
all enhanced individuals

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:49.100
to at least register with the government,

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:51.650
whether they are using
their powers or not,

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.810
which sounds a lot like the internment

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:56.958
of the Japanese in World War
II under executive order 9066

00:07:56.958 --> 00:07:58.640
by President Roosevelt.

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:01.770
That executive order was tested
at the Supreme Court level

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:05.230
in a court case Korematsu,
and the Supreme Court did not

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:09.370
overrule the executive order,
which interned the Japanese.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:11.900
Korematsu is still good law.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:14.370
That being said, I doubt
the Supreme Court would

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:18.260
rule the same way today,
despite the fact that the ruling

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:19.690
has never been overturned.

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:23.070
But in any event, it seems
like this is a clear violation

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:25.450
of the fourth and fifth
amendment protections

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:27.640
and a requirement for due process.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:30.830
Number three, monitoring
of enhanced individuals.

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:33.370
This seems like a clear
fourth amendment problem.

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:35.007
The Sokovia Accords state, and I quote,

00:08:35.007 --> 00:08:37.060
"Those with innate powers must also wear

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:39.180
tracking bracelets at all times..."

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:42.020
The problem is warrantless
monitoring without

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:44.500
probable cause; just because someone is an

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:47.040
enhanced individual would be a clear

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.880
fourth amendment violation,

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.750
a violation of the right to privacy,

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.900
being enhanced doesn't
necessarily mean that you have

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.700
probable cause to monitor them.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:57.830
And it would be crazy to have
a blanket monitoring system

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:00.300
that monitored everyone
in the United States

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:01.450
without probable cause.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:04.590
So it's very good the U.S.
government has never had

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:06.360
a program like that,

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:09.985
to monitor people without probable cause.

00:09:09.985 --> 00:09:11.960
(loon singing)

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.387
The Sokovia Accords also state that,

00:09:13.387 --> 00:09:15.070
"Those with innate powers must submit

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.910
to a power analysis, which
will categorize their

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.350
threat level and determine
potential health risks..."

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:23.360
This feels like a huge violation
of the right to privacy.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:24.940
The government can't just go around doing

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:27.000
medical examinations of
individuals just because

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.540
it feels like it or because
it's in the public interest.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:33.200
People have individual rights
specifically to protect

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:35.840
them from this kind of invasive testing.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:38.250
And additionally, it would
probably be a violation

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:40.370
of Tony Stark's intellectual property.

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:42.910
Even if he hasn't patented
the Iron Man suit,

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:45.000
it would probably be a trade secret,

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.450
and the compelled power
analysis would probably violate

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:51.600
his IP rights to the suit that he created.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:53.240
- It's working, we're safe.

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:54.270
America is secure.

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:55.130
You want my property?

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.260
You can't have it.

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:59.120
- Number four, the second
amendment's individual

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:00.330
right to bear arms.

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:02.840
While this is still a
huge point of controversy,

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:04.370
in recent Supreme Court precedent,

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.430
in the District of Columbia vs. Heller,

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.490
the Supreme Court confirmed
that the second amendment

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:11.910
does provide an individual
right to bear arms.

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:15.700
So, what is the threshold
for Iron Man, Falcon,

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:19.020
and War Machine to be able
to use their inventions

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:20.930
that they created effectively,

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:24.150
the Iron Man suits or the Falcon machinery

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:27.540
are just arms that they have created

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:30.130
and certainly, in some circumstances,

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:33.150
you are allowed to an individual
right to bear those arms.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.550
Now obviously, individuals are not allowed

00:10:35.550 --> 00:10:38.330
to have military hardware,
but the Sokovia Accords

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:41.490
don't make it clear where the
individual right to bear arms

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.910
starts and where the exclusion
of military technology

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:47.540
kicks in and how that would
apply to the individuals

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:51.664
who are not innately
enhanced, but have created

00:10:51.664 --> 00:10:55.150
an enhanced suit for themselves.

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:57.811
- I have successfully
privatized world peace.

00:10:57.811 --> 00:10:59.520
(Crowd clapping)

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:01.790
So given the make up of
the current Supreme Court

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:04.610
and the deference shown to the
individual right to bear arms

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:06.517
under the second
amendment, you can bet that

00:11:06.517 --> 00:11:10.400
the Sokovia Accords probably
run afoul of that right

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.680
under the Constitution as well.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:15.360
Number five, a violation of
the freedom to associate.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:18.540
The Sokovia Accords apply
to all of the Avengers,

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:20.920
even those who are not enhanced,

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:23.760
effectively preventing
them from being a member

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.670
of this community or group.

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:28.000
Now the first amendment is most famous for

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.940
the individual right to freedom of speech,

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:33.510
but the lesser known right
of the first amendment

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:36.170
is the right to voluntarily associate.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:39.010
And the Sokovia Accords
prevent individuals

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:42.230
from associating with
the private organization

00:11:42.230 --> 00:11:45.070
called the Avengers and
the private organization

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:45.990
called S.H.E.I.L.D.

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:47.990
Just because you are
an enhanced individual

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:50.060
doesn't mean you lack
first amendment rights

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:53.410
to be a part of the group that
you want to participate in.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:56.150
Number six, violation of
the freedom to travel.

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:57.937
The Sokovia Accords state, and I quote,

00:11:57.937 --> 00:12:00.570
"Any enhanced individuals
who sign are prohibited

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:03.770
from taking action in any
country other than their own,

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:05.590
unless they are first
given clearance by either

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:06.840
that country's government

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:09.690
or by a United Nation's subcmomittee..."

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:12.530
- Think of it this way, your
school has rules, right?

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:15.020
Like you can't draw on the walls.

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:17.490
Well your daddy went to
Germany and drew on the walls

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:20.090
with Captain America,
and that was a violation

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:23.720
of Article 16, paragraph
three of the Sokovia Accords.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:26.250
- Now the defined term taking action

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:28.000
can be read very broadly.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:30.150
Would that prohibit all of the Avengers

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:33.470
from setting foot in
any particular country

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:35.560
without getting the United
Nations subcommittee

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.200
to allow them to travel?

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:39.970
And would it prevent them
from traveling domestically

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:40.803
in the United States?

00:12:40.803 --> 00:12:43.000
If it does, that's clearly a violation

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.760
of the privileges and immunities clause

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:46.180
of the U.S. Constitution.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:48.670
And not to mention, the
violation of various

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:51.330
International laws that
allow freedom of travel,

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:54.100
particularly between the U.S. and E.U.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:57.120
I think that this is a
poorly drafted statement,

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:00.250
and it shows how important it is to define

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:01.600
the terms that you're dealing with,

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:03.680
because otherwise, people
will read them broadly,

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:05.710
when they're written
broadly, and it can have

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:07.100
unintended consequences.

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:09.470
Which takes me to problem number seven,

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:10.630
which is vagueness.

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:12.470
There is a constitutional
rule that requires

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:15.580
criminal laws to state
explicitly and definitively,

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:18.100
what conduct is punishable.

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:19.990
Criminal laws that
violate this requirement

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:22.520
are said to be void on vagueness grounds.

00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:25.920
The vagueness doctrine is based
on the due process clauses

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:28.860
of the fifth and 14th
amendments to the Constitution.

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:30.860
And I think that there's
a big problem here

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:33.470
in terms of what the enhanced individuals

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:37.240
are being accused of; vague
terms like taking action,

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:39.540
vague terms as in what constitutes

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:41.970
an enhanced individual itself,

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:45.100
all of these are vagueness
issues that are probably

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:48.360
so vague as to run afoul
of the due process clauses

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:49.660
in the Constitution.

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:51.700
That's why you need lawyers
to draft these things,

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:55.160
not comic book artists, but I digress.

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:57.090
It takes me to issue number eight,

00:13:57.090 --> 00:13:58.950
which is imprisonment.

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:01.811
The Sokovia Accords effectively
treat enhanced individuals

00:14:01.811 --> 00:14:04.560
who fail to comply with
the Sokovia Accords

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:06.220
as enemy combatants.

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.730
Now it's one thing to
send enemy combatants

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:12.060
that are imprisoned in
a foreign theater of war

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:14.000
and send them to Guantanamo,

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:17.470
but it's another thing
entirely to send U.S. citizens,

00:14:17.470 --> 00:14:20.380
who were found in the United States,

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:23.970
to the equivalent of Guantanamo
on some Helicarrier someway.

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:26.100
This is a clear due process violation.

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:29.060
You can't just put people
inside of a Helicarrier

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:31.790
with no lawyer, no
arraignment, and no bail.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:33.700
That's clearly a sixth amendment violation

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:35.181
to the right to council.

00:14:35.181 --> 00:14:37.917
- You're not gonna put me in a prison.

00:14:37.917 --> 00:14:40.110
You're not gonna put
any of us in a prison.

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:42.670
- And the other side of the
coin in problem number nine,

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:45.330
which is forced conscription in to combat.

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:48.100
The Sokovia Accords
appear to force certain

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:50.197
enhanced individuals in to fighting

00:14:50.197 --> 00:14:52.929
for the U.S. government
in certain times of war,

00:14:52.929 --> 00:14:54.950
effectively the draft,

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:58.040
but it's another thing
entirely to seek out

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:00.430
certain individuals specifically,

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:02.510
and then force them in to combat

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:03.970
on behalf of the government.

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:05.680
This seems like a clear violation

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:07.970
of the 13th amendment's prohibition

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:09.930
against involuntary servitude.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:12.250
You might recall that we
fought a real civil war

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:16.000
to prevent involuntary
servitude and slavery,

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:18.660
and forcing enhanced individuals to fight

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:21.770
for the government seems to run
afoul of those prohibitions.

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:23.570
Which takes me to problem number 10,

00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:26.140
and the biggest constitutional violation,

00:15:26.140 --> 00:15:28.730
the violation against habeus corpus.

00:15:28.730 --> 00:15:31.340
Habeus corpus is Latin
for produce the body.

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:33.407
And the Sokovia Accords
state, and I quote,

00:15:33.407 --> 00:15:36.160
"Any individuals who use
their powers to break the law,

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.830
including those who take
part in extra legal vigilante

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:42.370
activities or are otherwise
deemed to be a threat

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.810
to the safety of the general
public may be detained

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:46.487
indefinitely without trial."

00:15:46.487 --> 00:15:48.850
"If an enhanced individual
violates the Accords

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:51.450
or obstructs the actions of
those enforcing the Accords,

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:53.580
they may likewise be arrested and detained

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:55.750
indefinitely without trial..."

00:15:55.750 --> 00:15:57.550
You might see where this is going,

00:15:57.550 --> 00:16:00.856
but simply, detaining people
indefinitely without trial

00:16:00.856 --> 00:16:05.130
is the classic constitutional problem.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:08.600
And in fact, just simply
deeming someone a threat,

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:10.960
before they have committed
any kind of events

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:14.850
is like a precrime prohibition,

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:17.650
which again, runs afoul
of the Constitution.

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:21.120
The writ of habeus corpus
requires a person in custody

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:23.810
to be brought before a
court, provided a lawyer

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:26.700
if they can't afford
one, and to be protected

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:28.040
by the U.S. Constitution.

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:30.970
We fought the war of Independence
to have the protections

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:33.330
of the Constitution to prevent things like

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:37.280
indefinite imprisonment
for no reason whatsoever.

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:39.100
This violates the fourth
amendment which protects

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:40.940
people from arbitrary arrests.

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:42.990
It violates the fifth
amendment's protection against

00:16:42.990 --> 00:16:44.550
being deprived of life,
liberty, and property

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:45.880
without due process.

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:48.410
And it violates the sixth
amendment's right to council

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:49.740
and a trial.

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:51.860
There's actually very few
parts of the Constitution

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:55.300
that this part of the Sokovia
Accords don't actually

00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:57.500
violate, and that's why the lawyers

00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:01.215
are the real superheroes
in the Marvel Universe.

00:17:01.215 --> 00:17:03.810
(patriotic music)

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:06.760
So in thinking about this
Ultron Vision problem

00:17:06.760 --> 00:17:09.550
a little bit more, Tony created Vision,

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:13.200
Vision is Tony's property, his chattel,

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:16.923
so legally speaking,
Vision is like Tony's dog.

